This is my first hardware based project, the idea is simple:

you have 8 buttons, that can be programmed to do whatever you want (except commit tax evasion)

theres another button to change the profile you are on

and finally theres a screen that will display the profile you are on, and can display 
whatever you want on it.

what functionality i have now:
    -able to read input from buttons from the pi pico, and display which buttons are pressed
    -able to create a basic json file which stores profile and button info

what functionality im working on now:
    -more fleshed out json files
    -being able to create and save profiles
    -make decisions on button presses based on current profile

what functionality is planed in future:
    -allow buttons to do a range of things like:
        -work with OBS to change scenes, mute, ect.
        -open programs, pause and play music.
        -and other things that i cant think of
    -add code to work with display (plan to use a 16x2 lcd as a start, may upgrade to 20x4)
    -create a CLI to make it easy to update profiles
    -once basic functionality is finished, add 8 buttons to the pico 
    -support for both window and linux

may also work on a gui for it, but eh